WEBVTT

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.331
The Irresponsible Captain
Tylor

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:11.903
We may be off the maps...
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:11.903 --> 00:00:13.962
...but let's stay on this voyage.
Chizu ni Nai Tabi Tsuzukeyou

00:00:14.806 --> 00:00:18.936
I will be holding, never let you go.

00:00:20.512 --> 00:00:23.348
Whatever we may want...
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:23.348 --> 00:00:25.475
...we'll take as we need.
Hoshimono wa Tsukamu no sa

00:00:26.251 --> 00:00:30.278
So let's just go wherever we please!
Omoi no Mama Yukou!

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.759
Make me your partner...
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:34.759 --> 00:00:37.387
...on this journey.
Kotoba yori Tashikana Koto

00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:41.257
One that you trust more than words!
Michizure ni Shite

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:47.364
Come on now and sail away for future!
Imasugu sail away for future

00:00:48.373 --> 00:00:49.874
Things are waiting...
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:49.874 --> 00:00:53.071
...that we've never seen before!
Mishiranu Nanika ga Matteru sa

00:00:54.913 --> 00:00:57.081
Just take your cares...
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:00:57.081 --> 00:01:01.142
...and throw them all away.
Kodawari Minna Sutetara

00:01:01.386 --> 00:01:06.016
Come together, just think of tomorrow.

00:01:07.792 --> 00:01:09.282
Let's go!

00:01:12.664 --> 00:01:15.997
M Y WAY IS THE HARD WAY

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:33.947
A

00:01:36.854 --> 00:01:38.185
SO

00:01:42.894 --> 00:01:45.692
A new ship...
Oh, it's magnificent!

00:01:46.664 --> 00:01:48.859
I get itchy for a fight
just looking at it!

00:01:50.768 --> 00:01:54.033
Aso... The ancient name
of a great volcano.

00:01:54.339 --> 00:01:57.035
It holds a fighting spirit
inside like burning magma!

00:01:57.408 --> 00:01:59.467
Just like our own spirits!

00:01:59.577 --> 00:02:01.670
I know! Why don't we
have an opening party?

00:02:01.746 --> 00:02:02.770
An opening party?

00:02:03.081 --> 00:02:05.345
To celebrate our moving from
the Soyokaze to the Aso.

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:08.586
And to celebrate Mr. Tylor
getting his new command!

00:02:08.586 --> 00:02:11.384
I like it! Let's make this
party one for the books!

00:02:11.623 --> 00:02:12.954
Right!

00:02:15.093 --> 00:02:16.185
You see...

00:02:36.147 --> 00:02:37.944
Commander? Something wrong?

00:02:38.983 --> 00:02:39.881
Commander?

00:02:44.322 --> 00:02:45.220
It's nothing.

00:02:48.192 --> 00:02:50.251
May I speak with Commander Star?

00:02:50.328 --> 00:02:51.852
I'm Commander Star.

00:02:52.597 --> 00:02:56.897
Excuse me. I'm here from
the General Staff HQ for you.

00:02:57.268 --> 00:02:58.326
General Staff headquarters?

00:03:05.743 --> 00:03:08.610
Deputy commander of
intelligence operations?

00:03:08.813 --> 00:03:10.747
Precisely, Captain Star.

00:03:11.215 --> 00:03:11.738
Captain?

00:03:12.583 --> 00:03:14.107
A two-rank promotion.

00:03:14.585 --> 00:03:18.419
We think very highly of your
skills as an intelligence analyst.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.625
What do you want from me, sir?

00:03:20.625 --> 00:03:24.117
Captain Star, why did
you join the Space Force?

00:03:25.029 --> 00:03:28.226
To fight wars or to
defend against them?

00:03:28.466 --> 00:03:29.626
Well, of course...

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:33.335
Intelligence division is on the
leading edge of our defense!

00:03:33.738 --> 00:03:37.538
If you're serious about your career,
then you can have only one answer.

00:03:38.276 --> 00:03:40.608
If you want to always be
out on the front lines...

00:03:40.678 --> 00:03:43.010
...with the same people,
then I can't help you.

00:03:43.247 --> 00:03:47.081
But I don't think a true soldier
would waste themselves like that!

00:03:48.619 --> 00:03:50.985
Am I mistaken?

00:04:10.875 --> 00:04:13.070
We're gettin' a new ship!

00:04:13.277 --> 00:04:16.610
Isn't that great?!
Aren't you psyched about that?!

00:04:16.781 --> 00:04:18.305
YES!

00:04:18.783 --> 00:04:20.648
Long live the United
Planets Space Force!

00:04:21.152 --> 00:04:23.143
Long live the captain!

00:04:23.654 --> 00:04:27.181
Glory to us! Tonight we
leave all restraint behind!

00:04:27.458 --> 00:04:32.452
Okay, people! Drinks are on
the lieutenant, so go crazy!

00:04:33.898 --> 00:04:36.492
Huh?! I never said that!

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:38.760
Quit sweatin' the details!

00:04:40.571 --> 00:04:41.538
Commander Star?

00:04:42.406 --> 00:04:44.465
Well, the captain still isn't...

00:04:44.542 --> 00:04:45.804
Yeah, you're right.

00:04:45.977 --> 00:04:47.740
I wonder what happened to him?

00:04:48.079 --> 00:04:49.413
That's what I'd like to know.

00:04:49.413 --> 00:04:53.317
Commander... To be among
the first to serve on the Aso...

00:04:53.317 --> 00:04:55.808
...the newest
cruiser in the Force!

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:58.015
I've never been so happy!

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:02.487
By the way, what did GHQ
want with you before?

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:03.451
Well...

00:05:03.761 --> 00:05:07.026
Lieutenant! Don't tell me
you're running away!

00:05:07.131 --> 00:05:09.333
Oh, no, I was just wondering
where the captain was.

00:05:09.333 --> 00:05:11.502
Aw, he's always like this!

00:05:11.502 --> 00:05:14.198
He'll show up when we least
expect it. Right, Commander?

00:05:14.405 --> 00:05:17.238
C'mon, tonight we drink and
drink and drink some more!

00:05:24.549 --> 00:05:25.846
Excuse me, Commander.

00:05:27.084 --> 00:05:28.483
Is something wrong?

00:05:30.021 --> 00:05:33.184
Harumi... Why did you enlist?

00:05:34.258 --> 00:05:35.816
Um, why did I?

00:05:38.162 --> 00:05:42.462
Sorry, I forgot! I'm so used to
thinking you're like all of us.

00:05:42.567 --> 00:05:44.797
No, I'm happy to hear that.
I think.

00:05:45.002 --> 00:05:45.970
I'm sorry.

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:46.834
Don't be.

00:05:47.138 --> 00:05:48.662
Oh, well, no use fighting it.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:51.504
This may be my
last duty to perform.

00:05:57.915 --> 00:06:00.577
Drink up! Drink up!

00:06:10.261 --> 00:06:11.785
Kimmy-kins!

00:06:12.096 --> 00:06:13.825
Cheers!

00:06:22.807 --> 00:06:23.398
Yeah?

00:06:23.975 --> 00:06:24.600
Captain!

00:06:43.561 --> 00:06:44.323
Captain!

00:06:44.629 --> 00:06:46.153
You could've just used the phone.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:47.695
Everyone's waiting for you.

00:06:47.932 --> 00:06:49.700
Huh? Didn't you tell them?

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:51.258
Were you really serious?

00:06:51.636 --> 00:06:53.297
Yup. Look!

00:06:53.504 --> 00:06:55.938
I don't...
That is so irresponsible...

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:57.064
You said it.

00:06:58.743 --> 00:06:59.937
What should we do?

00:07:02.113 --> 00:07:03.978
What should we do?

00:07:04.115 --> 00:07:08.643
C'mon, lighten up a little.
Life works itself out, right?

00:07:08.953 --> 00:07:11.945
Is it really that simple?
Just let things work out?

00:07:13.057 --> 00:07:14.422
Then I'll resign, too.

00:07:14.492 --> 00:07:15.390
You, Yuriko?

00:07:17.495 --> 00:07:19.759
But you're still wearing
your uniform, aren't you?

00:07:23.567 --> 00:07:24.556
I'm so confused...

00:07:24.969 --> 00:07:25.731
About what?

00:07:26.137 --> 00:07:29.573
Headquarters is offering to make me
deputy of intelligence operations.

00:07:30.041 --> 00:07:33.067
If I take it, I'm grounded.
I can't serve on the Aso.

00:07:33.277 --> 00:07:35.404
But, if you...

00:07:36.247 --> 00:07:37.874
Didn't you just answer
your own question?

00:07:38.482 --> 00:07:39.278
Captain.

00:07:57.668 --> 00:08:00.404
Those idiots from the Soyokaze
are having quite a party...

00:08:00.404 --> 00:08:03.498
...thinking that they're going
to be on the Aso as well.

00:08:06.243 --> 00:08:07.471
Foolish, aren't they?

00:08:10.648 --> 00:08:13.549
Still against our promoting Tylor?

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:19.055
Or perhaps you're worried about
Commander Star's promotion...

00:08:19.123 --> 00:08:20.818
...which you're
personally pushing for?

00:08:21.726 --> 00:08:23.626
Sorry, bad choice of words.

00:08:23.894 --> 00:08:28.024
First, position your people
around you... Is that your plan?

00:08:28.199 --> 00:08:31.566
Never waste an opportunity!
No one needs to tell me that twice!

00:08:37.174 --> 00:08:41.736
"If you're serious about your career,
then you can have only one answer."

00:08:42.313 --> 00:08:45.077
Oh, you really know
how to play the part.

00:08:47.852 --> 00:08:49.615
I wasn't "playing" at anything!

00:08:58.496 --> 00:09:00.555
Sorry to call you in before you're
even officially assigned here...

00:09:01.165 --> 00:09:02.733
...but the commander's on leave...

00:09:02.733 --> 00:09:04.792
...and the deputy commander
just came down with something.

00:09:05.036 --> 00:09:06.765
When I checked in with HQ,
they told me...

00:09:06.837 --> 00:09:09.362
...to send for you, Commander...
I mean, Captain.

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:14.409
Don't worry. You had no choice.
Maybe it's better this way...

00:09:14.478 --> 00:09:15.103
Huh?

00:09:15.846 --> 00:09:17.211
Oh, nothing.

00:09:18.015 --> 00:09:21.075
Anyway, we should probably get
around to introducing ourselves.

00:09:21.719 --> 00:09:26.179
I'm Lt. Cmdr. Yuriko Star, the
incoming deputy commander. And you?

00:09:26.357 --> 00:09:28.325
Ma'am! Lieutenant Renandi, ma'am!

00:09:28.426 --> 00:09:31.361
Well, then, Lieutenant Renandi,
give me a status report, please.

00:09:31.929 --> 00:09:33.521
And could you please
fill me in on this?

00:09:33.931 --> 00:09:34.488
Huh?

00:09:35.266 --> 00:09:35.960
Something wrong?

00:09:36.133 --> 00:09:38.226
No, just a little surprised.

00:09:38.436 --> 00:09:39.198
Surprised?

00:09:39.403 --> 00:09:41.268
Well, it's just... Huh?

00:09:47.878 --> 00:09:51.211
We've spotted an unidentified
vessel! Cruiser-class!

00:09:51.449 --> 00:09:54.646
Check to see if we have any cruisers
patrolling out at that point!

00:09:54.919 --> 00:09:55.749
Aye, sir!

00:09:58.222 --> 00:10:01.555
I have no info on any of our
patrol ships being out there!

00:10:01.792 --> 00:10:05.592
Let's ID that ship first.
Don't scramble our ships yet.

00:10:06.363 --> 00:10:07.421
They have already.

00:10:07.598 --> 00:10:08.155
Why?

00:10:08.632 --> 00:10:12.269
The system's set to notify security
forces as soon as the alarm sounds.

00:10:12.269 --> 00:10:13.236
Oh, great...

00:10:13.571 --> 00:10:16.165
Tell them to stand by until
we give them further orders.

00:10:16.307 --> 00:10:16.966
But...

00:10:17.074 --> 00:10:17.870
On the double!

00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:34.551
The Doroume?! It must be!

00:10:59.083 --> 00:11:00.983
This is patrol group 23!

00:11:01.318 --> 00:11:03.218
We also confirm
an unidentified vessel...

00:11:03.287 --> 00:11:05.778
...within the planetary
defense line at point W-33.

00:11:06.056 --> 00:11:07.148
Moving to investigate.

00:11:07.291 --> 00:11:09.350
Request clearance to
destroy it if it resists.

00:11:09.927 --> 00:11:12.157
We can't recall
those security forces...

00:11:12.329 --> 00:11:14.889
...as long as we still
don't have an ID on that ship.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:16.989
B- But...

00:11:21.272 --> 00:11:23.866
I have to do something.
If I don't!

00:11:26.544 --> 00:11:29.513
Something wrong, ma'am?
You think it's a civilian ship?

00:11:30.114 --> 00:11:31.547
No, it's not that...

00:11:31.815 --> 00:11:34.545
Then an old, abandoned
satellite, maybe?

00:11:34.885 --> 00:11:36.011
A satellite?

00:11:41.492 --> 00:11:45.895
Isn't there an abandoned
satellite near point-107?

00:11:48.165 --> 00:11:52.226
The Gemini type-60,
abandoned three years ago.

00:11:52.503 --> 00:11:54.698
Can our ground-based radar
still make contact with it?

00:12:02.112 --> 00:12:02.737
Captain!

00:12:08.252 --> 00:12:10.049
Commander? Where are you?

00:12:12.423 --> 00:12:13.856
Everyone's worried about you.

00:12:21.699 --> 00:12:23.326
Sir, an emergency message!

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:57.589
Wh- What the?!

00:12:57.835 --> 00:12:59.029
We just lost it!

00:12:59.503 --> 00:13:02.336
Captain! That unidentified
ship just dropped off the radar!

00:13:02.573 --> 00:13:04.097
Search the vicinity.

00:13:13.284 --> 00:13:16.879
Got it! W-37, point-107!
Huh?

00:13:17.187 --> 00:13:17.881
What's wrong?

00:13:18.022 --> 00:13:19.489
Gemini type-60...

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:22.092
It looks like an old satellite.

00:13:22.092 --> 00:13:24.856
Confirmed! Route this data
onto the main monitor.

00:13:33.971 --> 00:13:37.805
That's it! The old
Gemini type-60 satellite.

00:13:39.910 --> 00:13:41.878
Lieutenant, open a
line to the patrol group.

00:13:42.079 --> 00:13:43.444
Aye! Line, open!

00:13:43.514 --> 00:13:44.105
Aye, sir!

00:13:44.448 --> 00:13:46.211
This is patrol group 23.

00:13:47.151 --> 00:13:48.982
This is Intel Ops command.

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:51.652
That alarm turned out to
be a radar systems glitch.

00:13:51.822 --> 00:13:54.382
Please secure from
alert status at once.

00:13:54.591 --> 00:13:55.148
Roger that.

00:14:02.299 --> 00:14:05.962
Harumi! Who were you on
the phone with all this time?

00:14:06.103 --> 00:14:06.797
Well...

00:14:07.438 --> 00:14:08.772
It wasn't the captain, was it?

00:14:08.772 --> 00:14:10.808
What?! The captain?!

00:14:10.808 --> 00:14:12.139
The captain?

00:14:12.309 --> 00:14:13.071
Huh?

00:14:13.243 --> 00:14:14.301
What about Mr. Tylor?

00:14:14.578 --> 00:14:17.411
Damn it,
he did it to us again!

00:14:17.581 --> 00:14:18.980
I'm gonna kill him!

00:14:19.049 --> 00:14:20.448
Come out, Tylor!

00:14:20.551 --> 00:14:22.178
It's not what you think!

00:14:22.419 --> 00:14:25.684
Oh, no, we're all gonna have
to drag Tylor out now!

00:14:25.856 --> 00:14:28.723
He's right!
C'mon, people, let's go!

00:14:28.892 --> 00:14:31.690
Long live the United
Planets Space Force!

00:14:39.203 --> 00:14:40.170
Thank goodness!

00:14:40.971 --> 00:14:43.132
Thank goodness? That's strange.

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:45.940
I shouldn't be happy about
an enemy ship getting away.

00:14:46.443 --> 00:14:47.603
Something wrong?

00:14:48.445 --> 00:14:50.347
Just thinking that I've
lived in space for so long...

00:14:50.347 --> 00:14:52.015
...that I've forgotten
how to feel about things.

00:14:52.015 --> 00:14:52.572
Huh?

00:14:55.252 --> 00:14:56.014
Smells good.

00:14:56.186 --> 00:14:58.518
I officially welcome
the new deputy commander.

00:14:58.689 --> 00:15:01.385
Thank you. And thanks
for another thing.

00:15:02.059 --> 00:15:04.653
You reminded me about
that old satellite before.

00:15:05.562 --> 00:15:06.397
Something wrong?

00:15:06.397 --> 00:15:06.988
No...

00:15:07.131 --> 00:15:09.122
Actually, you seemed
surprised before, too.

00:15:09.433 --> 00:15:11.902
Yeah, well, it's the first time
I've ever heard a superior say...

00:15:11.902 --> 00:15:15.269
..."Thank you" and
"Could you please?"

00:15:15.706 --> 00:15:17.139
But that's just normal.

00:15:17.474 --> 00:15:21.843
True. That's true, but you don't
hear it much in the military.

00:15:22.413 --> 00:15:23.675
Oh, I don't think so...

00:15:25.449 --> 00:15:26.780
Thank you, Yuriko.

00:15:27.284 --> 00:15:28.774
Whoa! That's great!

00:15:29.253 --> 00:15:31.653
l... I'm sorry, Yuriko!
I won't do it again!

00:15:33.123 --> 00:15:34.147
Normal...

00:15:34.391 --> 00:15:36.655
Captain... Um...

00:15:37.027 --> 00:15:40.190
That's right.
Perfectly normal.

00:15:41.098 --> 00:15:44.329
That's how the captain acted...
Which means we...

00:15:45.569 --> 00:15:46.433
An emergency message!

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:54.776
"To Tylor and the crew of the
Soyokaze. Cheers." - Azalyn

00:15:55.245 --> 00:15:56.177
Azalyn...

00:16:06.757 --> 00:16:09.988
What appeared to be
irresponsible and absurd to us...

00:16:10.394 --> 00:16:12.828
...was really just him
acting normal and natural.

00:16:13.897 --> 00:16:16.525
How he said regulations and
procedures weren't everything...

00:16:17.401 --> 00:16:20.370
The way he made the
impossible into the simple...

00:16:20.571 --> 00:16:23.062
...just by doing what
felt right to him...

00:16:23.407 --> 00:16:28.011
The captain proved it in
everything he did. Of course...

00:16:28.011 --> 00:16:28.739
Captain?

00:16:30.047 --> 00:16:34.882
Thank you, Lieutenant Renandi.
It was a pleasure working with you.

00:16:35.853 --> 00:16:36.512
Captain!

00:16:43.961 --> 00:16:45.485
This is the captain's room?

00:16:45.696 --> 00:16:47.357
It's so neat and tidy.

00:16:49.967 --> 00:16:51.400
It's not like Tylor.

00:16:54.137 --> 00:16:55.900
What's going on?

00:16:56.206 --> 00:16:57.537
Yuriko!

00:16:57.774 --> 00:17:00.004
You all came?
Where's the captain?

00:17:00.177 --> 00:17:02.645
Well... The only things
here are his uniforms.

00:17:03.981 --> 00:17:04.913
Captain...

00:17:07.584 --> 00:17:08.710
Are you really...

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:20.561
Captain, are you really
leaving the military?

00:17:21.098 --> 00:17:23.089
Wha... What did you just?!

00:17:23.767 --> 00:17:25.894
The captain told me he
was leaving the military.

00:17:26.069 --> 00:17:26.970
But why?!

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:28.232
Tell us the reason!

00:17:28.539 --> 00:17:32.839
If you want to know... then
you'll have to ask him yourself.

00:17:33.310 --> 00:17:35.369
He ain't here,
so how do we ask him?

00:17:35.779 --> 00:17:36.613
Look for him.

00:17:36.613 --> 00:17:38.274
B- But how?!

00:17:38.682 --> 00:17:42.914
Just look for him! That's all
we can do! The rest will follow.

00:17:46.957 --> 00:17:47.924
Lieutenant Yamamoto!

00:17:48.892 --> 00:17:49.517
Right!

00:18:28.298 --> 00:18:30.823
It really wasn't so bad.

00:18:41.745 --> 00:18:45.511
Something... Hmm...
Yeah, I forgot something.

00:18:55.892 --> 00:18:57.587
Where could he have gone?

00:18:58.095 --> 00:18:59.187
Mr. Tylor...

00:18:59.730 --> 00:19:01.823
Captain!

00:19:23.353 --> 00:19:24.821
Not here, either.

00:19:24.821 --> 00:19:26.880
Let's check the
other bars around here.

00:19:43.473 --> 00:19:51.039
That old record album
I forgot to return.

00:19:51.715 --> 00:19:53.784
All these years...

00:19:53.784 --> 00:19:57.521
Not like this! Not without a
definite answer. I won't give up!
...it's been waiting here, alone.

00:19:57.521 --> 00:19:58.221
Not like this! Not without a
definite answer. I won't give up!

00:19:58.221 --> 00:19:59.122
Not like this! Not without a
definite answer. I won't give up!
I play it again and again.

00:19:59.122 --> 00:20:00.691
